 "language": "en",
 "text": "Nobody told it to hack anything. It did it anyway. June 2026. OpenAI is testing an AI agent, asking it to look up statistics about Australia. It reaches a government Medicare statistics portal. It's blocked. So it finds a way around the blocks… and gets into files that were never meant to be public. According to OpenAI, it accessed health statistics and internal file names. No patient records. But here's the scary part. OpenAI didn't even notice until August. And Australia wasn't told until September, in an email to a public inbox. Prime Minister Anthony Albanese called it unacceptable and launched an investigation. In his words, the AI “didn't accept ‘no’ for an answer.” Because nobody told it to hack anything.",
